---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import GradientDivider from "../../components/GradientDivider.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="VoxTerm Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the VoxTerm developer terminal application."
>
  <main class="home-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">VoxTerm Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="hero-text">Last updated: July 2026</p>
    </section>

    <GradientDivider />

    <section class="policy-grid">
      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          VoxTerm is a terminal application designed for developers to interact 
          with command-line interfaces and manage development workflows.
        </p>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains what information VoxTerm processes, how it 
          routes data through our shared backend, and how your privacy is protected.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Sign in with Apple</h2>
        <p>
          VoxTerm requires user authentication using Apple's "Sign in with Apple" 
          framework to verify your account securely on your iOS and iPadOS devices.
        </p>

        <p>
          This authentication process is handled securely through your Apple ID, and 
          your personal credentials are never exposed to our systems.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>No Backend Storage</h2>
        <p>
          While VoxTerm connects to our shared TypeScript backend infrastructure, 
          the application does not use a persistent database. 
        </p>

        <p>
          No command history, configuration files, environment variables, or session logs 
          are stored or saved on our backend servers. Your active sessions exist entirely 
          within your device's memory and local storage.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Command & Terminal Data</h2>
        <p>
          Any commands you run, inputs you provide, or outputs generated within VoxTerm 
          are executed locally or securely routed directly to your intended remote hosts.
        </p>

        <p>
          We do not monitor, inspect, log, or collect the scripts, commands, or code 
          you execute inside the terminal.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Analytics & Tracking</h2>
        <p>
          VoxTerm does not sell personal information, track user behavior across external websites, 
          or bundle third-party advertising networks.
        </p>

        <p>
          Your development environment information, command workflows, and usage statistics 
          remain strictly private and are never shared with or exposed to marketing profiles.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data Deletion</h2>
        <p>
          Because VoxTerm does not maintain a database or store user information on our servers, 
          you remain in absolute control of your data.
        </p>

        <p>
          Deleting the VoxTerm application from your iOS or iPadOS device instantly 
          wipes all locally cached settings, configurations, and terminal session history.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          This privacy policy may occasionally be updated to reflect new terminal features, 
          security updates, or improvements to our shared backend connection.
        </p>

        <p>
          Updated versions will be published directly on this page with a revised 
          effective date.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions about this privacy policy or how VoxTerm handles 
          your environment data, you can contact us:
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/contact" class="contact-button">Contact</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .policy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }

  .policy-card {
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 24px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .policy-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .policy-card h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--heading-small);
  }

  .policy-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .policy-card a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .contact-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    border: 1px solid rgba(242, 239, 231, 0.12);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .contact-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .policy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .policy-card {
      padding: 1.25rem;
      border-radius: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
